  "id": "structural-integration",
  "term": "structural integration",
  "definition": "Structural integration refers to the way separate regions of the cerebral cortex are built into an interconnected whole. In this historical usage, it means that distant areas working together are anatomically linked by association fibres, creating mutual dependence in their activity and in disease.",
